<title>SOUTH KOREA: Korea Flour says buys 16,400 T of U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Korea Flour says buys 16,400 T of U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Korea Flour Milling Corp said on Wednesday it bought 16,400 tonnes of U.S. wheat from Japanese trading house Itochu Corp.</p>
<p>Early Wednesday, traders said the company had sought 16,700 tonnes of U.S. wheat, but a Korea Flour official corrected later the amount to 16,400 tonnes. The company official also said arrival was set to the western port city of Mokpo.  </p>
<p>The company official said shipment was slated for January 20-February 20 from the Pacific Northwest.</p>
<p>Details for the results by a trader source are as follow:</p>
<p>  Type of Wheat	     Tonne	Price/T (FOB)</p>
<p>  Soft White		  6,000	 $152.12</p>
<p>(protein max 10.5%)</p>
<p>  Soft White		  3,000	 $145.13</p>
<p>(protein max 9.5%)</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter	   3,700	 $184.63</p>
<p>  Dark Northern Spring    3,700	 $185.37</p>
<p>(and/or Northern Spring)</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
